@startuml INA700_ports_mapping_comms
' INA700 - coordinate, communication and UI ports
' Author: Suraj Karki
' Course: INA700 - AI-based pick and place

title INA700 - coordinate, comms and UI ports

' ObjectSelector and the rest of the layering are in
' pi-01-architecture.puml. Only the adapters the station runs are
' drawn here: the identity mapper and the loopback robot exist for
' the tests and are not in the cell.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam nodesep 14
skinparam ranksep 34
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam class {
  BorderColor #333333
  BackgroundColor #FDF6E8
  BackgroundColor<<port>> #EAF2FB
}

interface SceneCalibrator <<port>> {
  +{abstract} update(frame) : bool
  +{abstract} is_ready : bool
}
interface CoordinateMapper <<port>> {
  +{abstract} to_world_xy(point) : (float, float)
  +{abstract} is_calibrated() : bool
}
interface RobotTransport <<port>> {
  +{abstract} start()
  +{abstract} send(message)
  +{abstract} receive(timeout_s) : str [0..1]
  +{abstract} close()
  +{abstract} is_connected : bool
}
interface View <<port>> {
  +{abstract} render(snapshot)
  +{abstract} run()
}

class ArUco {
  -dictionary_name : str
  -marker_length_mm : float
  +detect(img) : (corners, ids)
  +draw(img, corners, ids)
  +corners_for_id(corners, ids, id)
  +pixel_mm_ratio(corners) : float
}

class ArucoCalibrator {
  -marker_length_mm : float
  -marker_centre_xy_mm : (float, float)
  -marker_angle_deg : float
  -y_axis_flipped : bool
  -scale_tolerance : float
  +update(frame) : bool
  -_scale_is_plausible(matrix, scale) : bool
}

class "homography_mapper.project()" as project <<utility>> {
  +project(matrix, point) : (float, float)
}
note right of project
  One definition of the projection:
  [x' y' w']T = H . [u v 1]T, then
  x = x'/w', y = y'/w'.
end note

class MutableHomographyMapper {
  -matrix : 3x3
  -lock : RLock
  +set_matrix(matrix, scale)
  +scale_px_per_mm : float [0..1]
  +to_world_xy(point) : (float, float)
}
class TcpServerTransport {
  -host : str
  -port : int
  -buffer : str
  +start()
  +send(message)
  +receive(timeout_s) : str [0..1]
}
class MessageCodec {
  +encode_pick(target) : str
  +encode_quit() : str
  +decode_reply(raw) : CycleOutcome
  -_guard_length(message)
}
class RobotCommander {
  -reply_timeout_s : float
  +__call__(target) : CycleOutcome
}

class TkView {
  -budget_ms : float
  -preview_max_width : int
  +render(snapshot)
  +run()
  -_handle_cycle_click()
  -_render_preview(preview)
  -_draw_pose(canvas, detection, scale)
  -_tick()
}
class ConsoleView {
  +render(snapshot)
  +run()
  -_print_scene()
  -_watch_status()
}

ArucoCalibrator ..|> SceneCalibrator
ArucoCalibrator *-- ArUco : detects with
ArucoCalibrator --> MutableHomographyMapper : refreshes every frame

MutableHomographyMapper ..|> CoordinateMapper
MutableHomographyMapper ..> project : projects with

TcpServerTransport ..|> RobotTransport
RobotCommander --> RobotTransport
RobotCommander *-- MessageCodec

TkView ..|> View
ConsoleView ..|> View

note bottom of ArUco
  Carried forward from Exercise 2 with the same
  responsibility, and living in adapters/detection.
  The calibrator USES it rather than extending it:
  detecting a marker and building a coordinate
  frame out of one are two different jobs.
end note

note bottom of MessageCodec
  A RAPID string holds 80 characters.
  _guard_length fails loudly here rather than
  truncating silently on the robot.
end note

' Stack the concrete classes so the diagram is not one wide strip.
ArUco -[hidden]down- ArucoCalibrator
ArucoCalibrator -[hidden]down- project
project -[hidden]down- MutableHomographyMapper
MutableHomographyMapper -[hidden]down- TcpServerTransport
TcpServerTransport -[hidden]down- MessageCodec
MessageCodec -[hidden]down- RobotCommander
RobotCommander -[hidden]down- TkView
TkView -[hidden]down- ConsoleView

@enduml
